      "text": "To find\n\n\\[\n\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\dotsm \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 99 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix},\n\\]\n\nwe start by analyzing the matrix product of two \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrices. Let's denote each matrix in the product as \\(A_n\\), where\n\n\\[\nA_n = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThe product of these matrices will be another \\(2 \\times 2\\) matrix. We will calculate this product step-by-step.\n\nFirst, consider the general form of the product of two matrices of the form \\(A_n\\) and \\(A_m\\):\n\n\\[\nA_n = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad A_m = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & m \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nTheir product is computed as follows:\n\n\\[\nA_n A_m = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & m \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nBy matrix multiplication, the element in the first row and first column is:\n\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 1 + n \\cdot 0 = 1,\n\\]\n\nand the element in the first row and second column is:\n\n\\[\n1 \\cdot m + n \\cdot 1 = m + n.\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and first column is:\n\n\\[\n0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 = 0,\n\\]\n\nand the element in the second row and second column is:\n\n\\[\n0 \\cdot m + 1 \\cdot 1 = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the product matrix \\(A_n A_m\\) is:\n\n\\[\nA_n A_m = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & m + n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to multiply this result by the next matrix in the sequence, \\(A_{n+1}\\):\n\n\\[\nA_n A_m A_{n+1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & m + n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} A_{n+1}.\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, we calculate the product \\(A_n A_m A_{n+1}\\):\n\n\\[\nA_n A_m A_{n+1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & m + n \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & (m+1) + (n+1) \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nThe element in the first row and first column is:\n\n\\[\n1 \\cdot 1 + (m + n) \\cdot 0 = 1.\n\\]\n\nThe element in the first row and second column is:\n\n\\[\n1 \\cdot (m+1) + (m+n) \\cdot 1 = m + 1 + m + n = 2m + n + 1.\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and first column is:\n\n\\[\n0 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 0 = 0.\n\\]\n\nThe element in the second row and second column is:\n\n\\[\n0 \\cdot (m+1) + 1 \\cdot 1 = 1.\n\\]\n\nThus, the product matrix \\(A_n A_m A_{n+1}\\) is:\n\n\\[\nA_n A_m A_{n+1} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2m + n + 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNotice that when we continue this pattern, each time we introduce a new increment, the pattern forms a superposition where the second row and first column element adds the increment. Specifically:\n\n\\[\nN = 1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + 99,\n\\]\n\nIf we sum this, we get the sum of the first 99 positive integers, which is:\n\n\\[\nN = \\frac{99 \\cdot 100}{2} = 4950.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final matrix is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 4950 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}}.\n\\]",
